          %h2#references References
          %p The cumulative hierarchy made its first appearance in
          %ul
            %li
              D. Mirimanoff,
              %em Les antinomies de Russell et de Burali-Forti et le problème fondamental de la théorie des ensembles
              , L’enseignement Mathématique
              %strong 19
              (1917) pp.37-52. (
              %a{:href => "http://retro.seals.ch/cntmng?pid=ensmat-001:1917:19::9"}> pdf
              ; 19,4MB)
          %p Another historically important contribution is
          %ul
            %li
              Dana Scott,
              %em Axiomatizing Set Theory
              , pp.207-214 in
              %em Axiomatic Set Theory
              \- Proc. Symp. Pure Math.
              = succeed "," do
                %strong 13
          %p A modern textbook account can be found e.g. in
          %ul#Kunen
            %li
              Kenneth Kunen,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Set Theory: An Introduction to Independence Proofs
          %p For algebraic set theory consult the following monograph
          %ul#JM
            %li
              André Joyal and Ieke Moerdijk,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Algebraic Set Theory
